# Every committed text file is LF, per EVANS_TEXT_FORMAT (the character floor):
# the least tolerant consumer sets the law, and here that is Swift — it treats
# "\r\n" as one grapheme, so a CRLF fixture parses as garbage, not an error.
* text=auto eol=lf

# The fidelity fixtures are LF data — never let a CRLF-writing tool (a stdlib
# csv.writer defaults to CRLF per RFC 4180) slip a carriage return into the tree.
*.csv text eol=lf
